\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {2.2}Overview of the Model}{3}{subsection.2.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall architecture of GHXTox. GHXTox adopts a hierarchical dual-level fusion design. The task-adaptive 1D sequence expert extracts toxicity-related sequence features with a LoRA-fine-tuned ProtT5 encoder and a bidirectional Mamba network, followed by three-seed ensembling and out-of-fold (OOF) Platt calibration to produce $p_{\mathrm  {1D}}$. The sequence-enhanced 3D structural expert extracts multi-scale structural information through an ESM2-enhanced sequence encoder, a pLDDT-aware equivariant graph neural network, full-atom chemical-site modeling, and an availability-masked conformer residual branch. Within this expert, sequence and spatial residue representations are integrated through pLDDT-aware cross-attention to produce $p_{\mathrm  {SE3D}}$. The two expert probabilities are fused with frozen weights of 0.62 and 0.38, and the final toxicity decision is obtained with a threshold of 0.4977.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{Overall architecture of GHXTox. GHXTox adopts a hierarchical dual-level fusion design. The task-adaptive 1D sequence expert extracts toxicity-related sequence features with a LoRA-fine-tuned ProtT5 encoder and a bidirectional Mamba network, followed by three-seed ensembling and out-of-fold (OOF) Platt calibration to produce $p_{\mathrm {1D}}$. The sequence-enhanced 3D structural expert extracts multi-scale structural information through an ESM2-enhanced sequence encoder, a pLDDT-aware equivariant graph neural network, full-atom chemical-site modeling, and an availability-masked conformer residual branch. Within this expert, sequence and spatial residue representations are integrated through pLDDT-aware cross-attention to produce $p_{\mathrm {SE3D}}$. The two expert probabilities are fused with frozen weights of 0.62 and 0.38, and the final toxicity decision is obtained with a threshold of 0.4977}{figure.caption.2}{}}
